							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">and while im at it.......<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">i think immortal technique&#039;s sentiments toward independent labels (not talking about massline but record labels were what he was talking about and i feel it&#039;s a good analogy) are also applicable to many revolutionaries</div><br /><br />no matter how intelligent, motivated and convicted immortal technique may be, lets set something straight here. personally, i think its unfair to even try and make the connection between what an MC is saying on wax and revolutionaries. REAL revolutionaries are killed, crippled and imprisoned everday around the world fighting LITERALLY, not figuratively or creatively, for what the believe in. thats why I have nothing but the utmost respect for the peopl ei fought overseas, because they are the manifestation in the EXTREME or a self motivated person standing the hard stance for what they believe in. Th Black Panther Party for self defense is the last thing comparable to a revolutionary group america has seen, and the countless militia gfroups in iraq and afghansitan are examples of what a real revolutionary stands for. even though i dont agree with them, i respect them.<br /><br />do you think Immortal Technique would be willing to die, lose an arm or leg or be permanently crippled or spend the rest of his life in prison due to his convictions about independant vs. major label music? no. not even &quot; i doubt it&quot;, hell no he wouldnt.<br />i totally dig the point your making, and IM NOT coming at you on the argumentative level, i just think that&nbsp; a lot of cats toss the word &quot;revolutionary&quot; around and to them its an abstraction or an empty metaphor repeated over and over again in popular media and college classes and music, when the reality is that the true revolutionary is to be feared, honored, respected, and taken very, very seriously.<br /><br /><br />but im rambling....<br /></div>
