							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">okay, good point. reagrdless of the methods used to achieve the end result, do you think its remotely fair to compare someone like immortal technique to a revolutionary?<br />maybe the underlying factor is risk. immortal technique takes no risk in making staunchly political records, outside of sales. <br />im not sure what the exact defenition of a revolutionary is, and theres a lot of grey area here, but i do think that theres a huge difference between immortal technique making a politically charged record and bobby hutton being murdered by the police.</div>
